course: dictionary
lesson: 11086
title: Words for direction
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You can often work out a word from the words around it. Westward looks like west with ward added, and ward tells you the direction is towards. So westward means towards the west. «The Black Death spread from Central Asia westward along trade routes» tells you it moved towards the west.
explain: Westward can be an adjective, which describes a noun: «the westward journey» tells you what kind of journey it was. It can also be an adverb, which tells you how something moves: «they sailed westwards» tells you which way they sailed. Some people in the UK spell the adverb westwards, with an s.
explain: Try swapping your meaning into the sentence. «The sun appears to move westward across the sky» still makes sense if you say «The sun appears to move towards the west across the sky». If your swap makes sense, you have probably found the right meaning.
fact: Westward means going towards the west.
fact: Westward is an adjective in «the westward journey» and an adverb in «sailed westward».
fact: «Westwards» is the UK spelling of the adverb, and it means the same thing.
fact: «Westward expansion» is a phrase from American history: settlers travelled west across North America in wagons, and this also took land from Native American peoples.
fact: Magellan's crew sailed westwards round the world with the Sun, so when they reached Spain their log was one day behind the date there.
exercise: «The Black Death spread from Central Asia westward along trade routes.» Which way did it spread? | Up into the mountains | *Towards the west | Under the sea | Towards the east
exercise: What does westward mean? | *Going towards the west | Lying under the sea | Going very fast | Going towards the north
exercise: «The sun appears to move ___ across the sky.» Which word fills the gap? | *Westward | Upward | Northward | Downward
test: In «the westward expansion», settlers travelled which way across North America? | Towards the south | Towards the ocean floor | *Towards the west | Round in a circle
test: Which spelling is the UK form of the adverb? | *westwards | westernmost | westward | westerly
exam: Which phrase uses westward as an adjective, describing a noun? | the sun moves westward | they sailed westward home | *the westward journey | travelled westwards
